### IsNull operator with findBy

Source: https://github.com/typeorm/typeorm/blob/master/docs/docs/working-with-entity-manager/3-find-options.md

Filters posts where the title is null. The TypeScript example uses the IsNull operator and the SQL query uses the IS NULL condition.

```typescript
import { IsNull } from "typeorm"

const loadedPosts = await dataSource.getRepository(Post).findBy({
    title: IsNull(),
})
```

```sql
SELECT * FROM "post" WHERE "title" IS NULL
```

--------------------------------

### QueryBuilder .where() with IsNull() operator

Source: https://github.com/typeorm/typeorm/blob/master/docs/docs/data-source/5-null-and-undefined-handling.md

Use the IsNull() operator to correctly match NULL values in QueryBuilder. This generates 'WHERE post.text IS NULL' and returns matching rows.

```typescript
import { IsNull } from "typeorm"

await dataSource
    .createQueryBuilder(Post, "post")
    .where({ text: IsNull() })
    .getMany()
// Generates: WHERE post.text IS NULL
```

--------------------------------

### Null Behavior: 'throw' (default)

Source: https://github.com/typeorm/typeorm/blob/master/docs/docs/data-source/5-null-and-undefined-handling.md

Configures the null behavior to 'throw' (the default), causing a TypeORMError to be thrown when a null value is encountered in a where condition. The example shows the error message and suggests setting 'invalidWhereValuesBehavior.null' to 'ignore' or 'sql-null' to handle null values.

```typescript
const dataSource = new DataSource({
    // ... other options
    invalidWhereValuesBehavior: {
        null: "throw",
    },
})

// This will throw an error
const posts = await repository.find({
    where: {
        text: null,
    },
})
// Error: Null value encountered in property 'text' of a where condition.
// To match with SQL NULL, the IsNull() operator must be used.
// Set 'invalidWhereValuesBehavior.null' to 'ignore' or 'sql-null' in data source options to skip or handle null values.
```

--------------------------------

### Configure invalidWhereValuesBehavior with null and undefined

Source: https://github.com/typeorm/typeorm/blob/master/docs/docs/data-source/5-null-and-undefined-handling.md

Sets invalidWhereValuesBehavior to transform null to SQL NULL and throw on undefined in where conditions. This combination allows explicit NULL searches while catching undefined programming errors.

```typescript
const dataSource = new DataSource({
    // ... other options
    invalidWhereValuesBehavior: {
        null: "sql-null",
        undefined: "throw",
    },
})
```

--------------------------------

### Using IsNull operator to match null values

Source: https://github.com/typeorm/typeorm/blob/master/docs/docs/data-source/5-null-and-undefined-handling.md

To match null values in where conditions, use the IsNull operator. This is the recommended approach for explicit null handling.

```typescript
const posts = await repository.find({
    where: {
        text: IsNull(),
    },
})
```
